// SYNTHESIZED, not captured live: issue #941 (Stage naming, green-finished, context brief,
// "Uses:" dependencies) needs a batch `task()` call whose owning assistant message actually
// echoes the call back as a `{"type":"toolCall",...}` content part -- the one shape neither
// `subagents.jsonl` nor `subagents-background-turn.jsonl` ever sent (both fixtures predate
// #941 and only ever drove the live `tool_execution_start`/`tool_execution_end` pair, never the
// message snapshot `build_assistant_items`'s own `"toolCall" =>` arm reads, per
// `src-tauri/src/omp/transcript.rs`), so neither exercises `message_id` ever getting stamped
// onto a `subagent` item (`subagent_items.rs`'s own `build_message_subagent_items`) -- without
// that stamp, `groupSubagentStages.ts` has no real Stage-boundary key to group on at all. Built
// directly from the documented wire contract (`transcript.rs`'s `"toolCall" =>` arm,
// `subagent_items.rs`'s `read_batch_context`/`build_message_subagent_items`/
// `apply_batch_task_result`/`apply_async_result_jobs`) for the R-lane driving issue #941's live
// check (`scripts/verify-941-stage-naming.mjs`). One user prompt, one agent turn, TEN serial
// Stages (ten separate `task()` batch calls, each its own assistant message/messageId) plus
// one plain, non-Stage `read` tool call -- deliberately never several separate prompt turns:
// `groupSubagentStages` runs once PER TURN (`Transcript.tsx`'s own `splitIntoTurns`, keyed on
// `kind: 'user'` items), so a later Stage's own "Uses:" dependency can only resolve against an
// EARLIER Stage inside the SAME turn's own `stages` array.
//
// Gate round 1 rewrite (item 15, new DOM contract): expanded from the original four Stages to
// seven Stages plus one bare tool call, covering: (1) Stage 3, no context and names sharing no
// prefix, a bare "Stage N" header; (2) Stage 4, a context whose first line exceeds 60 chars,
// exercising the exact truncate-with-ellipsis rule; (3) Stage 5, one failed agent among
// finished ones ("1 done, 1 failed"), and a SECOND occurrence of the agent name "Story559"
// (first seen in Stage 2) to exercise the "latest occurrence wins" dependency-resolution rule;
// (4) Stage 6, a SOLO Stage (one agent) with a real "Uses:" dependency on Stage 5's (not Stage
// 2's) Story559 occurrence, proving the solo path is no longer special-cased; (5) Stage 7, a
// long, multi-line context (with its own Markdown heading) that exceeds the ~6-line/144px cap,
// and a SELF-referencing `agent://LongCtxA` (one of Stage 7's own agents) that must be dropped,
// never shown in Stage 7's own "Uses:"; (6) a plain `read` tool call, never wrapped in a Stage,
// for the "tool rows stay neutral, never green" regression guard.
//
// Gate round 2 rewrite (items 10-12): Stage 7's own heading (and a new focusable Markdown link)
// were moved NEAR THE END of its context (several plain bullet points first) so the overflow/
// clipping test can prove both are genuinely clipped out of view AND out of the Tab order while
// collapsed (`StageContextBrief.tsx` no longer applies `inert` to the whole container -- only an
// overflowing focusable descendant gets `tabindex="-1"`, restored on expand). Three new Stages:
// (7) Stage 8, NO context, two agent names sharing a 3-char prefix ("PfxOne"/"PfxTwo") and
// nothing else to label from -- the `sharedNamePrefix` fallback, "Stage 8 · Pfx", never
// exercised before gate round 2; (8) Stage 9, a SOLO Stage with NO context at all -- its own
// agent name ("SoloBare") becomes the WHOLE label, "Stage 9 · SoloBare" (gate round 2 fix, item
// 1's "a solo Stage's own name is not just a bare 'Stage N' fallback" case, the no-context half
// of item 12's check -- Stage 6 already covers the with-context half); (9) Stage 10, a
// borderline-length single-paragraph context (no explicit line breaks) chosen to fit within the
// brief's own ~6-line/144px cap at a normal composer width but overflow once the window is
// narrowed, proving `StageContextBrief.tsx`'s own `ResizeObserver` genuinely re-measures on a
// real layout change rather than only once at mount (gate round 2 item 12's second check).
//
// Gate round 4 fix (issue #989, `agent://Main`): every `msg-ar1`..`msg-ar10` async-result
// message (both its own `message_start` and `message_end` frame) now carries `"display":true`,
// matching real omp (confirmed from the installed omp 18.11.1 binary's own embedded source,
// `packages/coding-agent/src/session/async-job-delivery.ts`'s job-delivery builder) -- this
// fixture previously omitted it, so no consumer could exercise the real display-leak bug
// `apply_message_snapshot`'s `"custom"` arm had on a `message_start` frame before the
// gate-round-3 short-circuit fix (`transcript.rs`). No OTHER consumer of this fixture reads or
// asserts on `display` for an async-result message (`verify-941-stage-naming.mjs` and its own
// panel/overflow helper scripts never touch Notice rows at all; `verify-941-part2.mjs`'s own
// Stage/panel/Up-next assertions don't either) -- an async-result message never renders a
// transcript row of its own regardless, so this addition changes nothing else.
// Additive extension (issue #991, 2026-10-18, gate follow-ups from the #941 lane's PR #979):
// one `{"__delay__": 1500}` inserted right after Stage 1's own assistant-message echo (so
// `message_id` is already stamped and Stage 1 genuinely renders as an open, running,
// two-member Stage) and before its `tool_execution_end` -- a deliberate ~1.5s window where
// Stage 1 is observably still running, for `scripts/verify-991-stage-focus.mjs`'s own
// keyboard-focus-survives-settling check. Nothing else in this file changes: every frame's own
// content, order, and timing (all of which wait on FINAL settled content, 30s timeouts) are
// unaffected by one extra ~1.5s pause this early in the tape. The PRODUCT change this delay
// exists to exercise (issue #991: `StageGroupRow`'s disclosure is now upward-only) DOES change
// what `verify-941-stage-naming.mjs`'s own expand-cycle assertions see for Stage 1 specifically
// (deterministically auto-open and staying open by the time they ever run, not closed) -- those
// assertions were updated to match (`assertExpandCycleByFinder`'s own doc comment has the full
// story); this fixture's own frames needed no further change beyond the one delay line above.
